# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GRWM AI — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Never commit `.env.local`.
#
# Note the split: the browser only ever needs the Convex URL. Every secret
# (Gemini, Context.dev) is set on the CONVEX deployment, because that is where
# the code using it runs. Nothing secret is exposed to the client, and none of
# these secrets belong in Vercel.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Convex ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Written automatically by `npx convex dev`.
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL` is the ONLY variable the frontend (and Vercel) needs.
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The variables below are set on the Convex deployment, NOT in this file:
#
#   npx convex env set GEMINI_API_KEY       ...
#   npx convex env set CONTEXT_DEV_API_KEY  ...
#
# For production, add `--prod`:
#
#   npx convex env set GEMINI_API_KEY ... --prod
#
# They are listed here so the required set is documented in one place.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Gemini ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The primary stylist: garment understanding, outfit choice, missing-piece
# reasoning and external product evaluation. If absent or failing, GRWM falls
# back to the deterministic recommendation engine and stays usable.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional. Defaults to a current Gemini model if unset.
GEMINI_MODEL=

# --- Context.dev ----------------------------------------------------------
# Live product intelligence for the Missing Piece Engine and "Should I buy
# this?". Server-side only. If absent or failing, GRWM falls back to product
# data captured from earlier real Context.dev extractions.
CONTEXT_DEV_API_KEY=

# --- Weather --------------------------------------------------------------
# None required. GRWM uses Open-Meteo, which needs no API key, and falls back
# to seasonal averages for the requested city if the call fails.

# --- Local scripts (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# `scripts/harvest-wardrobe-photos.mjs` and `scripts/extract-catalogs.mjs` read
# CONTEXT_DEV_API_KEY from this file when run locally. Not needed to run the app.
